"International AI Safety Report 2026 | International AI Safety Report (https://internationalaisafetyreport.org/publication/international-ai-safety-report-2026)\nciteturn909view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://internationalaisafetyreport.org/publication/international-ai-safety-report-2026\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 5524\nL0: cite0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com cite1†Skip to main content L1: \nL2: cite2†International AI Safety Report Menu\nL3: \nL4: Main menu\nL5: \nL6:   * cite3†About L7:   * cite4†Contributors L8:   * cite5†Expert Advisory Panel L9:   * cite6†Publications L10: \nL11: 3 February 2026 — Annual Report\nL12: # International AI Safety Report 2026\nL13: The second International AI Safety Report, published in February 2026, is the next iteration of the comprehensive review of latest scientific research on the capabilities and risks of general-purpose AI systems. Led by Turing Award winner Yoshua Bengio and authored by over 100 AI experts, the report is backed by over 30 countries and international organisations. It represents the largest global collaboration on AI safety to date.\nL14: Translated versions in the other 5 official UN languages can be found under the 'More Languages' button. The 'Extended Summary for Policymakers' can be found on the main 'Publications' page.\nL15: Download cite7†English L16: \nL17: More languages\nL18: \nL19:   * cite8†Français L20:   * cite9†Español L21:   * cite10†Русский L22:   * cite11†中文简体 L23:   * cite12†العربية L24: Y. Bengio, S. Clare, C. Prunkl, M. Murray,\nL25: M. Andriushchenko, B. Bucknall, R. Bommasani,\nL26: S. Casper, T. Davidson, R. Douglas,\nL27: D. Duvenaud, P. Fox, U. Gohar, R. Hadshar,\nL28: A. Ho, T. Hu, C. Jones, S. Kapoor, A. Kasirzadeh,\nL29: S. Manning, N. Maslej, V. Mavroudis,\nL30: C. McGlynn, R. Moulange, J. Newman, K. Y. Ng,\nL31: P. Paskov, S. Rismani, G. Sastry, E. Seger,\nL32: S. Singer, C. Stix, L. Velasco, N. Wheeler,\nL33: D. Acemoglu, V. Conitzer, T. G. Dietterich,\nL34: E. W. Felten, F. Heintz, G. Hinton, N. Jennings,\nL35: S. Leavy, T. Ludermir, V. Marda, H. Margetts,\nL36: J. McDermid, J. Munga, A. Narayanan, A. Nelson,\nL37: C. Neppel, S. D. Ramchurn, S. Russell,\nL38: M. Schaake, B. Schölkopf, A. Soto, L. Tiedrich,\nL39: G. Varoquaux, A. Yao, Y.-Q. Zhang, L. A. Aguirre,\nL40: O. Ajala, F. Albalawi, N. AlMalek, C. Busch,\nL41: J. Collas, A. C. P. de L. F. de Carvalho, A. Gill,\nL42: A. H. Hatip, J. Heikkilä, C. Johnson, G. Jolly,\nL43: Z. Katzir, M. N. Kerema, H. Kitano, A. Krüger,\nL44: K. M. Lee, J. R. López Portillo, A. McLysaght,\nL45: O. Molchanovskyi, A. Monti, M. Nemer, N. Oliver,\nL46: R. Pezoa, A. Plonk, B. Ravindran, H. Riza,\nL47: C. Rugege, H. Sheikh, D. Wong, Y. Zeng, L. Zhu,\nL48: D. Privitera, S. Mindermann, “International\nL49: AI Safety Report 2026” (DSIT 2026/001, 2026);\nL50: https://internationalaisafetyreport.org\nL51: Copy Citation\nL52: \nL53: Open Table of contents\nL54: ## Table of contents\nL55: \nL56: Contributors\nL57: \nL58: ##### Chair\nL59: \nL60: Prof. Yoshua Bengio, Université de Montreal / LawZero / Mila – Quebec AI Institute\nL61: ##### Expert Advisory Panel\nL62: \nL63: The Expert Advisory Panel is an international advisory body that advises the Chair on the content of the Report. The Expert Advisory Panel provided technical feedback only. The Report – and its Expert Advisory Panel – does not endorse any particular policy or regulatory approach.\nL64: The Panel comprises representatives nominated by over 30 countries and international organisation including from; Australia, Brazil, Canada, Chile, China, the European Union (EU), France, Germany, India, Indonesia, Ireland, Israel, Italy, Japan, Kenya, Mexico, the Netherlands, New Zealand, Nigeria, the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), the Philippines, the Republic of Korea, Rwanda, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, Singapore, Spain, Switzerland, Türkiye, the United Arab Emirates, Ukraine, the United Kingdom and the United Nations (UN).\nL65: The full membership list for the Expert Advisory Panel can be found here: cite5†https://internationalaisafetyreport.org/expert-advisory-panel L66: ##### Lead Writers\nL67: \nL68: Stephen Clare, Independent\nL69: \nL70: Carina Prunkl, Inria\nL71: \nL72: ##### Chapter Leads\nL73: \nL74: Maksym Andriushchenko, ELLIS Institute Tübingen\nL75: \nL76: Ben Bucknall, University of Oxford\nL77: \nL78: Malcolm Murray, SaferAI\nL79: \nL80: ##### Core Writers\nL81: \nL82: Shalaleh Rismani, Mila – Quebec AI Institute\nL83: \nL84: Conor McGlynn, Harvard University\nL85: \nL86: Nestor Maslej, Stanford University\nL87: \nL88: Philip Fox, KIRA Center\nL89: ##### Writing Group\nL90: \nL91: Rishi Bommasani, Stanford University\nL92: \nL93: Stephen Casper, Massachusetts Institute of Technology\nL94: \nL95: Tom Davidson, Forethought\nL96: \nL97: Raymond Douglas, Telic Research\nL98: \nL99: David Duvenaud, University of Toronto\nL100: \nL101: Usman Gohar, Iowa State University\nL102: \nL103: Rose Hadshar, Forethought\nL104: \nL105: Anson Ho, Epoch AI\nL106: \nL107: Tiancheng Hu, University of Cambridge\nL108: \nL109: Cameron Jones, Stony Brook University\nL110: \nL111: Sayash Kapoor, Princeton University\nL112: \nL113: Atoosa Kasirzadeh, Carnegie Mellon\nL114: \nL115: Sam Manning, Centre for the Governance of AI\nL116: Vasilios Mavroudis, The Alan Turing Institute\nL117: \nL118: Richard Moulange, The Centre for Long-Term Resilience\nL119: \nL120: Jessica Newman, University of California, Berkeley\nL121: \nL122: Kwan Yee Ng, Concordia AI\nL123: \nL124: Patricia Paskov, University of Oxford\nL125: \nL126: Girish Sastry, Independent\nL127: \nL128: Elizabeth Seger, Demos\nL129: \nL130: Scott Singer, Carnegie Endowment for International Peace\nL131: \nL132: Charlotte Stix, Apollo Research\nL133: \nL134: Lucia Velasco, Maastricht University\nL135: \nL136: Nicole Wheeler, Advanced